","text":"Whether the patient uses paracetamol","explanation":"This is not the main medication-specific concern."},{"id":"B","text":"History of seasonal allergies only","explanation":"This does not address the drug-specific operative issue."},{"id":"C","text":"Timing of the patient's last meal only","explanation":"Fasting requirements do not address iris effects."},{"id":"D","text":"Current or past tamsulosin exposure","explanation":"Tamsulosin is linked with intraoperative floppy iris syndrome during cataract surgery."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Notify the eye surgeon about current or previous tamsulosin use before cataract surgery.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ed-omnic-tamsulosin--7-day--tamsulosin_ifis","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ed-omnic-tamsulosin::tamsulosin_ifis"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ed-omnic-tamsulosin--standard--tamsulosin_ifis","answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Besides benign prostate symptoms, what is a selected emergency-department use of OMNIC — tamsulosin (oral)?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Helping passage of distal ureteral stones","explanation":"Medical expulsive therapy is an off-label use for carefully selected distal ureteral stones."},{"id":"B","text":"Dissolving bladder infection bacteria","explanation":"Tamsulosin is not an antibiotic."},{"id":"C","text":"Stopping gastrointestinal hemorrhage","explanation":"It has no hemostatic action."},{"id":"D","text":"Rapidly relieving pulmonary edema","explanation":"It is not a diuretic or pulmonary-edema rescue medication."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Recognize selected distal ureteric stones as an off-label ED use of tamsulosin.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ed-omnic-tamsulosin--7-day--tamsulosin_distal_stone","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ed-omnic-tamsulosin::tamsulosin_distal_stone"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ed-omnic-tamsulosin--standard--tamsulosin_distal_stone","answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A patient prescribed OMNIC — tamsulosin (oral) for a ureteral stone has fever 