n","explanation":"Bleeding risk and follow-up findings guide the protocol decision."},{"id":"C","text":"A normal peripheral pulse as the sole clearance criterion","explanation":"This does not exclude intracranial bleeding."},{"id":"D","text":"Improved speech as the sole clearance criterion","explanation":"Neurological benefit does not replace the protocol’s imaging requirement."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Follow post-thrombolysis monitoring/imaging before antithrombotic treatment.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"verified-alteplase-v35--advanced--alteplase_followup","points":1,"learningPointIds":["verified-alteplase-v35::alteplase_followup"],"answerKey":"B"}],"questionCount":7},{"id":"verified-alteplase-v35--7-day","itemId":"verified-alteplase-v35","itemType":"medication","title":"Alteplase (tPA)","stage":"7-day","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"persisted total deadline: 90 seconds multiplied by question count"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"show keys and all option explanations after submission","retestPolicy":"comprehensive memory retest; questions may repeat","questions":[{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"What is the principal mechanism of action of Alteplase (tPA)?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Activates receptors to promote glucose uptake","explanation":"This is a different pharmacological action. The drug’s action is: Alteplase promotes fibrin breakdown; it is distinct from preventing new coagulation."},{"id":"B","text":"Bronchodilation with a narrow therapeutic index","explanation":"This is a different pharmacological action. The drug’s action is: Alteplase promotes fibrin breakdown; it is distinct from preventing new coagulati