only after submission","retestPolicy":"same comprehensive exam and questions at every stage","questions":[{"stem":"Which structural/functional pattern characterizes the DCM teaching point?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Ventricular enlargement with impaired contraction","explanation":"A dilated weak pump can reduce cardiac output."},{"id":"B","text":"An isolated electrical AV block without a structural finding","explanation":"That does not define DCM."},{"id":"C","text":"Normal ventricular size with mandatory hypercontractility","explanation":"This is not the DCM pattern."},{"id":"D","text":"An isolated pulmonary airway narrowing","explanation":"That describes a different organ mechanism."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"DCM has ventricular dilation and weak systolic contraction.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-quick-dcm--comprehensive--point-70eb3ca4c427","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-quick-dcm::point-70eb3ca4c427"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"Which presentation is compatible with a dilated weak ventricle?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Only a painful Achilles tendon","explanation":"This points to another clinical issue."},{"id":"B","text":"Only oral white plaques","explanation":"This is not a characteristic cardiac presentation."},{"id":"C","text":"Only dry mouth with urinary retention","explanation":"This fits a different adverse-effect pattern."},{"id":"D","text":"Dyspnea, fatigue, congestion, and rhythm problems","explanation":"These are relevant HF/arrhythmia manifestations."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"DCM can present with HF and arrhythmia.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-quick-dcm--comprehensive--point-d4870f76f59b","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-quick-dcm::point-d4870f76f59b"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Which history is a recognized DCM-related contributor?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"A remote healed superficial abrasion","explanation":"This does not establish myocardial injury."},{"id":"B","text":"Myocarditis or a familial cardiomyopathy history","explanation":"These are recognized contributors."},{"id":"C","text":"A single normal ECG recording","explanation":"A normal recording is not an etiology."},{"id":"D","text":"An uncomplicated local fungal mouth infection","explanation":"This is not the named myocardial cause."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Myocarditis, inherited disease, or cardiotoxic exposures can contribute to a DCM phenotype.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-quick-dcm--comprehensive--point-7f76481a9a66","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-quick-dcm::point-7f76481a9a66"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which set contains recognized contributors to dilated cardiomyopathy?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Familial disease, myocarditis, cardiotoxic exposure","explanation":"All are listed contributors."},{"id":"B","text":"Pin-site irritation, fracture swelling, cast tightness","explanation":"These are limb-related concerns rather than the DCM contributor group."},{"id":"C","text":"Peptic ulcer, oral candidiasis, iron chelation","explanation":"These are not the listed DCM contributor group."},{"id":"D","text":"Peripheral neuropathy, tendon rupture, dry mouth","explanation":"These are adverse-effect patterns of other treatments."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Recognize familial, inflammatory, toxic, peripartum, and tachyarrhythmic contributors.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-quick-dcm--comprehensive--point-0515bc625040","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-quick-dcm::point-0515bc625040"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A DCM patient develops low urine output and confusion with cool skin. Which new problem is most concerning?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"A therapeutic increase in renal clearance","explanation":"Oliguria does not establish improved clearance."},{"id":"B","text":"A local IV-site problem as the established cause","explanation":"No local site findings explain the systemic pattern."},{"id":"C","text":"Low-output organ hypoperfusion","explanati