-external-fixator::point-c36801b639ea"],"answerKey":"C"},{"stem":"Which sequence provides a structured bedside review of an external fixator and the patient?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Patient name, bed number, billing, transport","explanation":"This is not a clinical fixation check."},{"id":"B","text":"Frame, stock cupboard, discharge, diet","explanation":"This is not the focused cue."},{"id":"C","text":"Pins, antibiotics, discharge, exercise","explanation":"This omits essential limb and frame assessment."},{"id":"D","text":"Limb, pins, frame, patient","explanation":"The cue begins with tissue safety before hardware and the wider patient review."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Use the limb–pins–frame–patient bedside structure.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-lesson-02-external-fixator--comprehensive--point-2db556f84025","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-lesson-02-external-fixator::point-2db556f84025"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Which pin-site change requires review?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"An unchanged frame shape with a clean site","explanation":"No new pin-site problem is established."},{"id":"B","text":"Increasing redness and new drainage with fever","explanation":"These are infection warning findings."},{"id":"C","text":"Improving local tenderness without other changes","explanation":"This does not identify the warning pattern."},{"id":"D","text":"An unchanged clean site without new pain","explanation":"This does not describe deterioration."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"New pin-site redness/drainage/fever can indicate infection.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-lesson-02-external-fixator--comprehensive--point-983b27d58dc1","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-lesson-02-external-fixator::point-983b27d58dc1"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which information determines the pin-cleaning product and schedule?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"A general preference for any household antiseptic","explanation":"Product choice must be c